+# Retained divergence and capture applicability
+
+CPU analysis on2026-11-16 used the actual CC Host on retained `ROOT/night-branch-engine-v2/run-001/cell-001-A/speed/stdout.log` and `cell-003-C/speed/stdout.log`. Four paired requests each contain128 generated IDs and finish `length`. All first differ at zero-based output index49, baseline10367 and candidate32187, following49 common IDs. They repeat a single prompt; they are not four independent workload cases. Full receipts, input IDs and SHA256 source-file identities are retained outside source at `ROOT/night-numerical-investigation-cpu-20261116/retained-first-divergence.json`. ROOT is `/home/user2/software-factory-spark-20261113`. This is new CPU analysis of historical GPU outputs, not a newly reproduced engine result.
+
+The initial development parser selected the DONE draft-count column as a finish value. It was corrected to the actual finish column and rerun under fresh Host idempotency keys; original development Host receipts remain in the owned ccstore. No source evidence was changed.
+
+The retained report identifies `/opt/strata/strata-dsv41 --serve`, DS4 engine kind, `--dspark none`, and prefill chunks256/1024. Inspect `ROOT/sources/strata-deepseek/src/dsv41/ds4_main.cpp`, SHA256 `fb3ff96a416b8efe077c5eecffd1bdbdf957ebc36cd8ae7f8ff86e50a4aa3973` at this development snapshot. The qualified source closure is `ROOT/projects/fixed-placement`, clean HEAD `89ae0ee6123597636ef162dec826230186c00f3b` (use its full retained build/source manifest identity); the same file hash also exists in `sources/strata-deepseek` at its different checkout revision. Equal main-file hashes do not establish equal whole-source closure. Existing `DS4_SERVE_DUMP` reads an opt-in file prefix (line529), opens `<prefix>.<request>.f32` after prompt consumption (1387), writes the prompt-final logit row, appends `m.logits` after each decode round (1462), then flushes at request completion (1467). It is raw float32, without a dimensions/provenance header. These are source-read findings, not a demonstrated capture run. The hook does not propagate all open/write/copy failures, so independent import must reject missing, truncated, nonfinite or dimension-inconsistent evidence.
+
+With drafting disabled, one completed plain decode round corresponds to one next-output row. A first-divergence replay can retain the original prompt boundary: run the original prompt, verify output IDs before step49 equal the frozen teacher prefix, then use row49. This is conditional same-history replay, not general forced replay; if earlier tokens differ from the frozen prefix, reject. Restrict one conversation, no images, no drafting, greedy decoding and explicit finite output limits. Keep request order/cache state identical or use fresh processes as separately declared treatment. Retain raw profile/build/model/tokenizer manifests. Captured and observer-disabled outputs/finishes must be checked before numerical or performance interpretation.
+
+Do not append49 generated tokens to the prompt and prefill them. That changes the historical prompt/decode boundary and may erase the state difference under investigation. Generic `strata-dgx-spark/src/program/generate.cpp` has `--tokens`, `--prefill-until` and `--dump-logits`, but these are not proof of applicability to the retained DS4 serve binary. Its native pack bypasses the dump-writing token loop. `STRATA_DUMP_FIRST_LOGITS` in that other path writes only the first verifier window and cannot establish output49 replay for this case.
+
+No retained full-logit vectors or observer-on/off evidence were found or manufactured. Common-history top choices, margins and numerical cause remain unknown until an admitted run captures and independently validates them. No new GPU run was launched for this package.
